  "sourceTitle": "Japanese Vegetable In Tempura Batter",
  "sourceText": "Japanese Vegetable In Tempura Batter\nBy: Anonymous\nPublished: Tuesday, December 1, 2009 - 11:41pm\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\n1 cup flour\n1 cup ice water\n1 slightly beaten egg\n2 tablespoons salad oil\n1/2 teaspoon each sugar and salt\nSliced zucchini\nSliced sweet potatoes\nSliced white potatoes\nCauliflower florets\nbroccoli florets\nPepper slices\nSliced Bermuda onions\nString beans\nMushrooms\n\nPreparation\n\n1 Beat together all ingredients - a few flour lumps should remain. Keep batter cool with one or two ice cubes in the batter. Dip vegetable in batter and fry in deep hot fat (360 to 365 degrees) until tender and brown.",
